{"step_index":302,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T21:05:53Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 3 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. LETS also have a landing page similar to netflix one which will allow users to either login or get started with the name of the streaming company \n2. Extend the existing StreamWave FastAPI/Vercel project by adding an original landing page, simulated subscription-payment process and paid-member access control.\r\n\r\nDo not rebuild or break the existing catalogue, music player, five-second movie preview, playback logging, API documentation or Vercel configuration. Inspect the existing project before changing anything.\r\n\r\nThis is an academic demonstration. Do not integrate a real payment gateway, transfer money or collect real financial information.\r\n\r\nLANDING PAGE\r\n\r\n1. Make `/` the public landing page and the first page encountered by visitors.\r\n2. Use the existing StreamWave logo and dark graphite, white and red brand colours.\r\n3. Use the supplied streaming-service screenshot only as inspiration for visual hierarchy. Do not copy Netflix branding, wording, copyrighted posters or exact layout.\r\n4. Create an original hero section using existing StreamWave catalogue artwork with a dark overlay.\r\n5. Use this main copy:\r\n\r\n   * Heading: “Zimbabwe’s stories, \n<truncated 5408 bytes>\n3. Review and refine the StreamWave landing page and simulated checkout created in the previous step.\r\n\r\nDo not change the working FastAPI architecture or payment-session logic unless necessary to fix a verified problem.\r\n\r\nLANDING-PAGE DESIGN\r\n\r\n1. Create a full-height hero section with a dark collage made only from the project’s