{"step_index":304,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T21:06:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T23:06:24+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T23:06:24+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py`\nTotal Lines: 538\nTotal Bytes: 19688\nShowing lines 265 to 295\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n265: \n266: \n267: # --- Public HTML Page Routes ---\n268: \n269: @app.get(\"/\", response_class=FileResponse, include_in_schema=False)\n270: async def serve_landing_page():\n271:     \"\"\"Serves the public StreamWave landing page.\"\"\"\n272:     landing_file = PUBLIC_DIR / \"index.html\"\n273:     if landing_file.exists():\n274:         return FileResponse(str(landing_file))\n275:     raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Landing page not found\")\n276: \n277: \n278: @app.get(\"/checkout\", response_class=FileResponse, include_in_schema=False)\n279: async def serve_checkout_page():\n280:     \"\"\"Serves the simulated academic checkout page.\"\"\"\n281:     checkout_file = PUBLIC_DIR / \"checkout.html\"\n282:     if checkout_file.exists():\n283:         return FileResponse(str(checkout_file))\n284:     raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Checkout page not found\")\n285: \n286: \n287: @app.get(\"/library\", response_class=FileResponse, include_in_schema=False)\n288: async def serve_library_page():\n289:     \"\"\"Serves the paid member catalogue library page.\"\"\"\n290:     library_file = PUBLIC_DIR / \"library.html\"\n291:     if library_file.exists():\n292:         return FileResponse(str(library_file))\n293:     raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Library page not found\")\n294: \n295: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":305,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T21:06:24Z","content":"I have resolved the `Landing page not found` error!\n\n### 🔍 Cause of the Error\nPreviously, `vercel.json` routed **every single URL** to the Python serverless function `app.py`. Inside Vercel's python function container, static files in the `public/` directory were not included inside Python's lambda sandbox.\n\n### 🛠️ Fix Applied\nI updated [`vercel.json`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/vercel.json) to use Vercel's recommended hybrid architecture:\n- **Backend API (`/api/*`, `/docs`)** -> Handled by Python FastAPI serverless functions.\n- **Frontend Pages (`/`, `/checkout`, `/library`, CSS, JS, MP4/WAV media)** -> Served directly by Vercel's Global Edge CDN for ultra-fast load times and zero cold starts!\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Push the Fix to GitHub & Vercel\n\nRun these commands in Command Prompt to push the updated configuration:\n\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"fix: Route /api/* to FastAPI and serve static frontend pages via Vercel CDN\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push origin main\n```\n\nYour live Vercel site (`https://streamwave-gamma.vercel.app`) will re-deploy and display your full landing page!"}
